Of course, we do not want to remain in the weaker invariant forever. But
how can we get back, if the Δ′enviroment is wrong? The trick is that we
have to wait until execution of the nested expression is finished. Then,
any resulting value can be typed with an empty Δ′enviroment:

\textbf{Lemma 16.} (\emph{Values do not borrow})\\
If Δ \textbar{} Γ ⊢\emph{v}, then ∅\textbar{} Γ ⊢\emph{v}.

