⊆fv(\emph{e})\emph{,y}. \textbf{Lemma 38.} (\emph{The eval context is
complementary to the tail context})\\
If \emph{e} = T {[}\emph{f} {]}, \emph{f} ∈\emph{f}and \emph{e} =
\emph{E}{[}\emph{f} (\emph{y};\emph{x}){]}, then \emph{E} = □.

