\textbf{Proof}. Our transformation follows the general framework of TRMC
where we use a defunctionalized

evaluation context (section 4.2 of {[}Leijen and Lorenzen 2023{]}). Note
that we generalize the (\emph{tlet}) and (\emph{tmatch}) rules of the
TRMC translation (figure 2 in {[}Leijen and Lorenzen 2023{]}) to a
(\emph{tctx}) rule. In particular, we include drops and frees in the
tail context. However, the correctness of

these additional cases is clear. We thus have
\emph{f}′(\emph{v}1;\emph{v}2\emph{,} H) −→∗\emph{w} by the correctness
of the context transformation and the context laws for defunctionalized
evaluation contexts.

