\textbf{Lemma 50.} (\emph{Associativity of joining heaps})

Let \emph{H}1 be a sound heap and \emph{H}2\emph{, H}3 be linear heaps.
Then (\emph{H}1 ⊗\emph{H}2) ⊗\emph{H}3 = \emph{H}1 ⊗(\emph{H}2
⊗\emph{H}3).

\textbf{Proof}. As before \emph{x} ∈dom((\emph{H}1 ⊗\emph{H}2)
⊗\emph{H}3) iff \emph{x} ∈dom(\emph{H}1), \emph{x} ∈dom(\emph{H}2) or
