⊗\emph{H}3)). Let us consider the reference count of one such \emph{x}
with reference count \emph{n, m, k} in \emph{H}1\emph{, H}2\emph{, H}3
respectively. Then:

\emph{n} + \emph{m} + \emph{k} −\#\emph{x}(\emph{H}1 ∩\emph{H}2)
−\#\emph{x}((\emph{H}1 ⊗\emph{H}2) ∩\emph{H}3) (1), reference count in
(\emph{H}1 ⊗\emph{H}2) ⊗\emph{H}3 = \emph{n} + \emph{m} + \emph{k}
−\#\emph{x}(\emph{H}1 ∩\emph{H}2) −\#\emph{x}(\emph{H}1 ∩\emph{H}3)
−\#\emph{x}(\emph{H}2 ∩\emph{H}3) + \#\emph{x}(\emph{H}1 ∩\emph{H}2
∩\emph{H}3) (2), lemma 48

