x} ↦→\emph{mv, z} ↦→\emph{k}+1\emph{w}) iff\emph{z} = fv(\emph{v})

\textbf{Lemma 53.} (\emph{Heap subtraction})

If \emph{H}1 and \emph{H}2 are linear heaps with roots Γ1\emph{,} Γ2 and
\emph{H}1 →\emph{H}2, then {[}\emph{H}1\emph{, H}2{]} is a linear heap
with

roots Γ2 −Γ1.
