\textbf{E.3} \textbf{Progress}

In this section we want to show that the heap semantics can progress if
the simple invariant

is true and operational semantics can progress. We assume throughout
that for any function

\emph{f} (\emph{y};\emph{x}) = \emph{e} ∈Σ, we have fv(\emph{e})
⊆\emph{y,x}. This is true if Σ is fully in-place:

