We define {[}H −\emph{x}{]}\emph{e} as the substitution which replaces
every variable \emph{y} ∈fv\uline{(}\emph{e}) −\emph{x} by
{[}H{]}\emph{y}. Notice that this is different from formally
subtracting\emph{x} from the heap ({[}{[}H{[}\emph{\uline{x}}{]}\emph{,}
H\emph{e}), since the substitution {[}H −\emph{x}{]}\emph{e} can still
work on children of\emph{x}, which might get deleted in
{[}H{[}\emph{x}{]}\emph{,} H{]}. Then:

